# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: open-ccs-bom-bricscad-windows-divergence — clautolisp's (open f "w,ccs=UTF-8") writes no BOM under the BricsCAD Windows dialect; BricsCAD V25 writes one
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-open-ccs-bom-bricscad-windows-divergence
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Context

Found 2026-10-08 while closing encoding-situations-cli-options (the BricsCAD
",ccs=" append measurement, job 17027935338). BricsCAD V25 on Windows writes
a byte-order mark for ",ccs=UTF-8" and ",ccs=UTF-16LE" (probe-open-encoding:
"A" e-acute "B" is 7 bytes with "w,ccs=UTF-8", 8 with "w,ccs=UTF-16LE" --
jobs 16968316289 and 17027935338), and an append with the same ",ccs=" adds
no second one (7 -> 9, 8 -> 10).

* Problem

clautolisp (2.3.9, =clautolisp-sbcl --dialect bricscad-v25=) writes no BOM:

#+begin_example
(setq f (open "ap.txt" "w,ccs=UTF-8")) (write-char 65 f) (write-char 233 f) (close f)
(setq f (open "ap.txt" "a,ccs=UTF-8")) (write-char 233 f) (close f)
  -> ap.txt = 41 C3 A9 C3 A9            (BricsCAD: EF BB BF 41 C3 A9 ... C3 A9)
(setq f (open "ap16.txt" "w,ccs=UTF-16LE")) (write-char 65 f) (close f)
(setq f (open "ap16.txt" "a,ccs=UTF-16LE")) (write-char 66 f) (close f)
  -> ap16.txt = 41 00 42 00             (BricsCAD: FF FE 41 00 42 00)
#+end_example

The append half already matches (no second BOM); the write half does not.
The spec's =*** clautolisp= note under ~open~ says the ",ccs=" suffix is
honoured silently under the Windows BricsCAD dialects for UTF-8 / UTF-16LE
("honoured, measured"), which suggests the same bytes.

* Proposal

Under the Windows BricsCAD dialects (product BricsCAD, platform Windows --
dispatch on product/platform, never on a dialect keyword), ",ccs=UTF-8" and
",ccs=UTF-16LE" on mode "w" (and on "a" creating a new, empty file -- not
measured; decide) write the BOM first; "a" on an existing file writes none.
Other dialects unchanged. Document it in the =*** clautolisp= section of
~open~ and the clautolisp user manual. (Not done on the measuring branch: no
clautolisp source changes were allowed there.)

* Acceptance criteria

- under bricscad-v25 (Windows), "w,ccs=UTF-8" of "A" e-acute -> EF BB BF 41 C3 A9;
  "w,ccs=UTF-16LE" of "A" -> FF FE 41 00; the appends add no BOM;
- other dialects byte-for-byte unchanged; builtin unit tests.
